  "tagline": "Sidecar-plus-object-storage layer giving Prometheus global queries, HA dedup and long retention.",
  "description": "Thanos extends existing Prometheus servers rather than replacing them. A sidecar uploads two-hour TSDB blocks to object storage, Store Gateways serve that history, the Querier fans PromQL out across every source and deduplicates HA pairs, and the Compactor downsamples old data. A Receive component also accepts remote write for push-based setups. A CNCF incubating project created at Improbable, it is a common choice for teams that want cheap long retention on S3 or GCS without moving to a fully centralised write path. The cost is many moving parts and query latency that depends on object-store reads.",
